{
  "acceptance": [
    "default (zstd) tsbs_devops load into InfluxDB gives dbgen row counts",
    "default port consistent between metadata and compose"
  ],
  "batch": {
    "batch_id": "load-path-live-fixes",
    "implementation_dependencies": [],
    "member_id": "influxdb-load-ignores-compressed-tsbs-files-20261106"
  },
  "context": "Priority medium: fails loudly, with a workaround (--compression none). Not fixed by the verifier.\n\nFixed in PR #3981 (merge c1a2dc186b). Verdict: PRE-EXISTING (7aa4a8b391, before #3952, reads only <table>.csv and loads nothing from zstd data). Before: 'no rows were loaded for any table'. After (default zstd data, port=8181 passed): cpu 172800, mem 172800, disk 345600, net 345600, tags 10 on influxdb:3-core; the load reads .csv/.zst/.gz/.bz2 through the shared compression handler (one file per table), checks written rows against source rows and the server count, and fails when nothing loads. The default-port inconsistency (8086 metadata vs 8181 compose) was split out by parent ruling to influxdb-default-port-8086-vs-compose-8181-20261106 and is not fixed here.",
  "description": "Found by live verification of #3952 on origin/develop 525361b2f8, influxdb:3-core.\n\nReproduction: `benchbox run --platform influxdb:core --benchmark tsbs_devops --scale 0.01 --phases generate,load --platform-option host=localhost --platform-option port=8181 --platform-option ssl=false --non-interactive` (default compression zstd gives cpu.csv.zst etc.).\nExpected: cpu 172800, mem 172800, disk 345600, net 345600 rows.\nActual: `Required benchbox tables are missing or empty after load: no rows were loaded for any table. Loaded tables: []` because InfluxDBAdapter.load_data looks only for data_dir/<table>.csv (benchbox/platforms/influxdb/adapter.py, around line 135) and skips the .csv.zst files. With `--compression none` the same load gives exact row counts (see item perf-questdb-influxdb-load-20261030 evidence). Also, the default port in platform metadata is 8086 while the compose stack and adapter default_service_port use 8181, so `--platform-option port=8181` is required. Pre-existing since the initial release (csv_path line dates from e0438e9932).\n\nSuspected: InfluxDBAdapter.load_data should resolve files through normalize_table_paths / the compression handler like other adapters.",
  "final_evidence": {
